" test/escaped_brackets_link.vader
" Link text may contain escaped brackets (`\[` / `\]`); the link must still
" render (delimiters and URL concealed) and end at the real closing `]`.
"
" Run with:
"   vim -u NONE -N +'set rtp+=.' +'runtime plugin/vader.vim' +'Vader! test/escaped_brackets_link.vader'

Given markdown (link with escaped brackets in text, plus a plain link):
  [Run \[dev me\] job - Databricks](https://example.com/run?o=1)
  [plain](https://example.com/plain)

Execute (set up markdown syntax):
  set filetype=markdown conceallevel=2
  unlet! b:current_syntax | runtime syntax/markdown.vim

Execute (URL of link with escaped brackets is concealed):
  let col = stridx(getline(1), 'https') + 1
  AssertEqual 'mkdURL', synIDattr(synID(1, col, 1), 'name')

Execute (opening bracket is a concealed delimiter):
  AssertEqual 1, synconcealed(1, 1)[0]

Execute (plain link still works):
  let col = stridx(getline(2), 'https') + 1
  AssertEqual 'mkdURL', synIDattr(synID(2, col, 1), 'name')
